OrionLayer open fix 86 — the fleet box's order buttons on the wire ("FBTN")
=========================================================================

Work order 229 Part C (the standing decision of 4 October 2026: an engine
change a part needs is made in that run — applied on `orionlayer-local`,
bundle in ~/claude/bundles/, nothing online, decision 85). orion2re on
`orionlayer-local`, on top of open fix 85. Every line under ORION2RE_EXT
(ext_api.cpp).

The fleet box offers ALL and up to five order buttons — Outpost, Colonize,
Engage, Transport, Attack Antares — each decided by
FLEETPOP::Set_Added_Button_Stuff_ (fleetpop.cpp:813-856) into
_fleet_box.*_btn_active and added as a field under CLOSE whose id only MOX
holds (Add_Added_Buttons_, :444-510; ALL :181-186). mainscr.cpp:3411-3500
answers a button only while its flag is set and its field is the input. A
client saw the fields' rectangles and could not say which was which, so
OrionLayer's fleet box offered no orders. The snapshot now carries "FBTN"
while the fleet box shows a stack on the galaxy map, after RFIT's place: a
version byte, the stack, its star, whether the player's combat ships there
ignore enemies (the bit Engage clears), then per button its flag and field.
Read only.

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
index 3831887d..fa797a35 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -1847,6 +1847,52 @@ static void SerializeState(std::vector<uint8_t>& buf,
         Write16(buf, COLREFIT::_first_ship);
         Write16(buf, COLREFIT::_n_ships_in_list);
     }
+
+    // 29. The fleet box's order buttons: "FBTN", written ONLY while the
+    //     fleet box (moveable box 2) shows a stack, after RFIT's place.
+    //     OrionLayer, open fix 86.
+    //
+    //     Which of ALL, Outpost, Colonize, Engage, Transport and Attack the
+    //     box offers is decided by FLEETPOP::Set_Added_Button_Stuff_
+    //     (fleetpop.cpp:813-856) into _fleet_box.*_btn_active, and each
+    //     button is a field whose id only MOX holds (Add_Added_Buttons_,
+    //     :444-510; ALL :181-186). mainscr.cpp:3411-3500 answers a button
+    //     only while its flag is set and its field is the input. A client
+    //     saw the fields' rectangles and could not say which was which. Per
+    //     button the flag and the field (-1000 when not added), in the
+    //     order above; then the stack's star and whether the player's
+    //     combat ships there ignore enemies (star.ignore_combat_ships, the
+    //     bit Engage clears, mainscr.cpp:3466-3471; 0xFF without a star).
+    //     Read only; nothing here changes the game.
+    if (current_screen == SCREEN_MAIN && MOVEBOX::Moveable_Box_Selected_(2) &&
+        MOX::_fleet_box_ship_stack >= 0 &&
+        MOX::_fleet_box_ship_stack < MOX::_ship_stack_count) {
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'F');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'B');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'T');
+        buf.push_back((uint8_t)'N');
+        Write8(buf, 1);                                   // block version
+        Write16(buf, MOX::_fleet_box_ship_stack);
+        const int16_t fbtn_star = HACCESS::Ship_Stack_Star_Id_(
+            MOX::_ship_stack_start[MOX::_fleet_box_ship_stack]);
+        Write16(buf, fbtn_star);
+        Write8(buf, (fbtn_star > -1 && fbtn_star < MOX::_NUM_STARS)
+            ? (uint8_t)((MOX::_star[fbtn_star].ignore_combat_ships >>
+                         (MOX::_PLAYER_NUM & 0x1f)) & 1)
+            : (uint8_t)0xFF);
+        Write8(buf, (uint8_t)(MOX::_fleet_movement_all_button > 0));
+        Write16(buf, MOX::_fleet_movement_all_button);
+        Write8(buf, (uint8_t)(MOX::_fleet_box.outpost_btn_active != 0));
+        Write16(buf, MOX::_fleet_box_outpost_button);
+        Write8(buf, (uint8_t)(MOX::_fleet_box.colonize_btn_active != 0));
+        Write16(buf, MOX::_fleet_box_colonize_button);
+        Write8(buf, (uint8_t)(MOX::_fleet_box.engage_btn_active != 0));
+        Write16(buf, MOX::_fleet_box_engage_button);
+        Write8(buf, (uint8_t)(MOX::_fleet_box.transport_btn_active != 0));
+        Write16(buf, MOX::_fleet_box_transport_button);
+        Write8(buf, (uint8_t)(MOX::_fleet_box.attack_btn_active != 0));
+        Write16(buf, MOX::_fleet_box_attack_button);
+    }
 }
 
